---

<section id="faq" class="section faq-section">
  <div class="site-shell faq-section__inner">
    <div class="faq-section__intro">
      <h2>FAQ</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-list">
      <details>
        <summary>I’m not naturally tidy. Will this even work for me?</summary>
        <div class="faq-item__content">
          <p>Yes – you’re exactly who I design for. I don’t expect you to become a different person or suddenly love cleaning. Instead, we plan the layout and storage so it’s easier for your natural habits to land in better places: clear drop zones, fewer surfaces that attract piles, and systems that are realistic for your actual energy level.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Will you tell me to get rid of lots of things?</summary>
        <div class="faq-item__content">
          <p>We’ll gently edit, but I’m not here to police your belongings. My focus is to make what you keep <strong>work harder</strong>: easier to find, easier to put away, and less visually overwhelming.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Do you do renovations or anything permanent?</summary>
        <div class="faq-item__content">
          <p>No. Everything I suggest is renter‑friendly and reversible – no walls down, no built‑ins, no drilling that will upset your landlord. We work with layout, movable furniture, lighting and storage you can take with you.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Do you only work in person? What if I’m moving soon?</summary>
        <div class="faq-item__content">
          <p>For Hong Kong rentals, I recommend in‑person sessions because moving things physically is a big part of the process. If you’re moving and don’t have access yet, we can do Session 1 online using your floor plan and photos, then do Session 2 in person after you move in.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Why bother, if it’s just a rental?</summary>
        <div class="faq-item__content">
          <p>A one‑year lease can feel temporary but it’s still a full year of your life. You wake up there, come home tired there, process big feelings there. When your flat doesn’t support you, you feel it every day. And even if you <em>do</em> care about how it looks, it can be hard to find the time, energy or clarity to turn it into a space that actually supports you.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>I live with a partner / roommates. Can we still do this?</summary>
        <div class="faq-item__content">
          <p>Yes. There will always be one main client and point of contact, but I’m happy to work in homes with more than one person. If we’re working on <strong>shared spaces</strong> (like the living room), I ask that everyone who uses them is aware of the project and joins at least part of Session 1 so we can make decisions that feel fair and realistic for everyone. If we’re only working on <strong>your private room</strong>, I’ll stay within that space.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq-section {
    background: var(--section-bg, var(--bg));
    border-top: 1px solid var(--section-border, rgba(199, 148, 92, 0.2));
    padding: 2.5rem 0 3rem;
  }

  .faq-section__intro h2 {
    margin: 0.35rem 0 0;
  }

  details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.08);
    padding: 0.75rem 0;
  }
  summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--section-heading, var(--heading));
    list-style: none;
  }
  summary::marker { color: var(--section-accent, var(--accent-teal)); }
  summary::after {
    content: "+";
    float: right;
    color: var(--section-accent, var(--accent-teal));
  }
  details[open] summary { color: var(--section-accent, var(--accent-teal)); }
  details[open] summary::after { content: "–"; }
  details p { margin-top: 0.5rem; color: var(--section-text, var(--text)); }
</style>

<script>
  // FAQ Accordion - only one open at a time
  const faqDetails = document.querySelectorAll('#faq details');
  
  faqDetails.forEach(detail => {
    detail.addEventListener('toggle', (e) => {
      if (detail.open) {
        // Close all other open details (accordion behavior)
        faqDetails.forEach(otherDetail => {
          if (otherDetail !== detail && otherDetail.open) {
            otherDetail.open = false;
          }
        });
      }
    });
  });
</script>
